  "title": "Adapter Pattern: Integrate a Cloud Service Provider",
  "language": "python",
  "difficulty": "core",
  "estimatedMinutes": 35,
  "instructions": "Wrap the third-party SDKs (`libraries/`, provided) behind the `CloudAdapter` interface. Implement `AWSCloudAdapter` and `GoogleCloudAdapter` in `adapters/` (call the SDK, map its response to the domain `Connection`), `CloudServiceImpl.create_connection` in `services/cloud_service_impl.py` (raise `UserNotFoundException(\"User not found\")` for an unknown user, otherwise delegate to the injected adapter) and `CloudController.create_connection` in `controllers/cloud_controller.py` (translate that exception into `ResponseStatus.FAILURE`).",
